From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 23:14:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] chimera: handle cursor and display power events

Consume Revdi events through the owned Rust API. Repack strided ARGB8888 cursor buffers into Vino cursor messages, account for the hotspot on movement, and replay mode activation or the dock-side blank sequence across DPMS transitions.

Complete unsupported DDC/CI reads explicitly with failure so the virtual I2C adapter cannot wait forever; full tunneled reads remain tied to the kernel control-reply parser.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
